body:
`DocumentType` is called out above as gaining these `ChildNode` methods, however testing this, the new APIs don't actually work on `DocumentType`

When attached its parent must be a `Document`, which causes `HierarchyRequestError`, and when detached it has no parent so these methods return early.

```js
let docType = document.implementation.createDocumentType("html", "", "");
docType.replaceWithHTMLUnsafe("<html><body>Example page</body>");
// throws a HierarchyRequestError

const docType = document.implementation.createDocumentType("html", "", "");
docType.parentNode; // null
docType.replaceWithHTMLUnsafe("<p>Hello</p>");
// doesn't throw, but doesn't do anything as returns early
```

Is that intentional and simply an acceptable consequence of matching the existing `ChildNode` API shape? Would it make sense to expose these methods via a mixin that only include `Element` and `CharacterData`, analogous to DOM's [`NonDocumentTypeChildNode`](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-nondocumenttypechildnode)?
